# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored and is the only place real
# keys belong; a key that reaches a commit is public from that moment and has to be
# rotated (CLAUDE.md).

# Model access, through OpenRouter's OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_MODEL=

# Supabase, for accounts and the library. Both come from the project's API settings.
# Leave them empty and Redline still runs: a Signer can bring a contract in and read what
# came out of it, with the account, the library and the red lines switched off and said
# to be switched off. Filling them in is what turns those on.
#
# The anon key is publishable and reaches the browser by design. It is safe there only
# because every table has row level security (supabase/migrations/), which is what stops
# one Signer's query from returning another's documents.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# tests/integration/signer-isolation.test.ts only. It creates and deletes accounts, so
# point it at a scratch project, never one holding real documents. With any of the three
# empty the suite skips and says which are missing — it never reports green unrun.
#
# The service-role key bypasses row level security. It is used there for fixture setup and
# teardown and for nothing else, and it is not read anywhere in the application.
SUPABASE_TEST_URL=
SUPABASE_TEST_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_TEST_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
